{
  "description": "Minimal regression test for fontanf/packingsolver issue #563, isolated from the original 56-shape union input. This single, valid (Shape::check() true, non-self-intersecting), 38-element concave shape with no holes is fed to compute_difference(shapes_1={shape}, shapes={}) (i.e. difference against nothing, which should return the shape unchanged). Root cause: Shape::find_point_strictly_inside() picks a probe point that is not actually inside the shape (it pairs the tangent point of a corner-fillet arc -- which only touches a sampled horizontal ray without crossing it -- with the next real crossing, as if both were real crossings), so compute_boolean_operation_component wrongly discards the one valid face and returns zero faces instead of one.",
